VALUES (601, '1', $t$ASK 601: a judge never runs the same model as a debater$t$,
  $t$A judge whose model is the same as either debater's model never sits: not on the panel, not as the reserve, and not as an alternate. This holds even when both debaters are Anthropic. The change goes LIVE (ruling 512). (plan rev 1, OBJECTIVE, ask601/w4/plan601.md 7aab840d)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 12:19 CST 2026-11-24 (n8n updatedAt 18:19:50Z) on the card "Write it" pressed 12:18 CST in W4's thread (Wall 11652; audit 41585). Database first: odv1_record_panel_alternates 39d84307 to ad0d9e9c (new guard G-SAME, after G1 and before G2); dash_judge_lineup caea9e6c to e19ac69b (drops a same-model seat with its reason). Engine ff7ab4cf to 21316a8e-9107-4ba7-8966-230d20ad2d3f: two nodes changed, Init Seats 7949df51 to 0579c436 (drops from the free seats a seat whose model equals a debater's, reason "runs the same model as a debater (<model>)") and Resolve Seats 767dc7b0 to ffb7b688 (a panel judge with a debater's model stops the run; the reserve and the alternates skip such a seat). Child ecdc6218 unchanged; no prompt text and no model setting changed; nothing deleted. W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11654). Shown in part by run 42283 (ODV1-42283-f584bu4b, debate_results b0ccda27, saved 13:48 CST 2026-11-24; Opus defender, Claude challenger): the judge order's alternates list names sonnet and the SEATED alternates are chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon, without sonnet (review_notes, Wall 11666); on run 42234, before the rule, sonnet was among the seated alternates. The dropped seat's reason line is not in review_notes; W4's offline replay of Init Seats gives "runs the same model as a debater (anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5)" (W4's replay, relayed in Wall 11669). Run 42283 ended with no verdict (the ASK 611 expression defect), so it is not a clean live run. The rule acts only when claude (anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5) debates another Anthropic model, the one pair of active seats that shares a model. Shown offline: of the 90 debater pairs the engine accepts, 88 are unchanged and 2 change (claude against opus, both ways: sonnet dropped). Open: two clean live runs (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); revert601_db.sql is not rehearsed; the manual entry's Limits line still says "not shown by a run" and is owed a one-pair revision on its own card. The engine manual entry was written by W3 on its own card (part 03.0 v303 at 13:07 CST, part 10.0 v304 at 13:52 CST; audit 41604). RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). No seated judge or alternate ran a debater's model, and the run was judged. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule asks, for ASK 601, for its both-Anthropic path only (W1's limit, Wall 11785); IN PART until the second (W1, Wall 11890). Seen and not part of the objective: the AGREEMENT block still asked the sonnet seat ("ACCEPT; may judge"), a cost only. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'. RUN REVISION 42528 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed, that a path is unexercised, or what objective_met is, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42528-dqwbcshc (debate_results e0e528d8, row saved 22:59 CST 2026-11-24; launch 22:26 CST, ended with success 23:42 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; every stage ran and no error row was written; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments and 659 enforcer rows stored; cost 11.1907). No judge ran a debater's model on a second pairing: hydrogen (the defender, on the panel list) and spark (the challenger, on the alternates list) are on the order and are not seated; no judgment or enforcer row names either model as a judge. This is a second live run with no issue for this ASK, on a pairing that is not both-Anthropic (the first: run 42373, both-Anthropic). W3 leaves objective_met 'in part' and status 'read back' because the row's other Open items stand: revert601_db.sql is not rehearsed and the manual entry's Limits line is owed its one-pair revision; and each of the two paths has one run. The row does not state the reason a seat was left out.$t$,
