es list names sonnet and the SEATED alternates do not; no seated judge or alternate runs a debater's model; the run was judged. The AGREEMENT block still asked the sonnet seat (\"ACCEPT; may judge\").", "source": "aar/w3/aar_run42373_draft6.md 6ef38f57 (W1 PASS Wall 11875), OBJECTIVE item 14; every RESULT there is from W3's SQL on the run's rows, 17:40 to 17:50 CST 2026-11-24, or from a seat's Wall post named there", "not_shown": "no panel send-back was sent in this run (AAR DEFECT 1); the n8n execution was not read by W3", "prior_case": "NO PROBE (the plan states no ASK 417 registry entry exists for seat selection). SHOWN IN PART by run 42283 (ODV1-42283-f584bu4b, debate_results b0ccda27, 13:48 CST 2026-11-24; Opus defender, Claude challenger): review_notes \"[JUDGE ORDER v2: panel list sol, sol62, spark; alternates list chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon, sonnet | SEATED: panel sol62, spark, sol; reserve none; alternates chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon]\"; sonnet is not seated. The reason line is not in the run's record; W4's offline replay of Init Seats gives it (W4's replay, relayed in Wall 11669). The run ended with no verdict, so it is not one of the two clean live runs, which are still owed."}, "source": "aar/w3/aar_run42528_draft2.md 87de2ee1 (W1 PASS Wall 11941), OBJECTIVE item 10; every RESULT there is from W3's SQL on the run's rows, 23:50 CST 2026-11-24 to 00:04 CST 2026-11-25, or from a seat's report named there"}$j$::jsonb,
